      "template": "Hi,\n\nPossible causes:\n1. Sudden load surge (RV AC startup, inverter inrush, water pump, etc.) where load current exceeds the battery's continuous discharge current.\n2. Charging system disconnecting — voltage falls from charge voltage back to open-circuit voltage.\n3. Loose terminals, cable oxidation, or excessive junction voltage drop.\n\nIf none of these explain it, contact us for a closer look.\n\nIf the battery is defective, please help provide: a clear photo of the top of the battery showing the serial number, and a photo of the whole battery.\n\nBest regards,\nLitime",
