      "template": "Hi,\n\nMain reasons:\n1. Long-term use in a high-temperature environment causes cell bulging.\n2. External devices (inverter, charger, MPPT, etc.) mounted too close — their heat softens the case so it can't hold the internal buffer compression, bulging the shell.\n\nNeither poses a safety risk and the battery can be used normally, but we recommend adjusting the installation and operating environment.\n\nIf the battery is defective, please help provide: a clear photo of the top of the battery showing the serial number, and a photo of the whole battery.\n\nBest regards,\nLitime",
