      "issue": "Outboard shows 0V / cuts out after ~30 min (e.g. Yamaha F70)",
      "summary": "Battery's 15V overvoltage protection + outboard's simple regulator -> mutual shutdown. Short-term: return.",
      "template": "Hi,\n\nThis is mainly due to differences in equipment: some outboards have a simpler or slower-responding voltage regulator. When our LiFePO4 battery is full, by design it enters overvoltage protection (threshold 15V) and the BMS quickly cuts the charging circuit to protect the battery. If the outboard's regulator keeps outputting current, voltage briefly rises because there's no consumption path. To protect itself, the outboard shuts down. This is the result of both protection mechanisms working — essentially to prevent overvoltage damage.\n\nBest regards,\nLitime",
