      "template": "WHAT'S HAPPENING\nYou connect a charger and nothing happens — no current, no rise in voltage.\n\nHOW TO DIAGNOSE\n1. Is the battery in voltage protection while the charger has NO activation function? (see the 0V entry)\n2. Is an external load connected? It can divert all the charging current so the battery never sees it.\n3. Are the terminals loose, aged, or corroded? Poor contact blocks charge.\n4. Measure the charger's open-circuit output — it should match the rated voltage (e.g. ~14.6V for a 12V LiFePO4 charger). No/low output points at the charger.\n\nFIX\n- Use a charger with lithium activation.\n- Remove or switch off external loads while charging.\n- Clean oxidised/corroded terminals and re-tighten to the manual's torque.\n- With an AC-DC charger, connect DC before AC. With MPPT/DCDC, confirm the PV source or main battery has enough energy.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENS\nEither the BMS is protecting and the charger can't wake it, the energy is being siphoned by a load, or resistance at the terminals is too high to pass charge current.\n\nHOW TO AVOID\nUse a proper LiFePO4 charger, keep terminals clean and torqued, and don't charge with a heavy load hanging off the same terminals.",
      "note": "",
