      "summary": "After full charge the app shows module voltage while the meter reads the whole PACK incl. BMS (0.5-0.7V gap) — normal, discharge to clear. If the meter reads very low (3-7V) and won't discharge, the app's discharge switch is OFF — turn it on.",
      "template": "WHAT'S HAPPENING\nThe app and your multimeter disagree — e.g. app 13.33V vs meter 12.8V, or app ~13.4V but meter reads only 3-7V with no output.\n\nHOW TO DIAGNOSE\n- Small gap (~0.5-0.7V) right after a full charge: the app shows the battery module voltage; the meter reads the entire pack including the BMS board, which has a protection-state offset.\n- Large gap with no discharge (meter 3-7V): the discharge switch in the app is turned OFF.\n\nFIX\n- Small gap: normal post-charge protection offset — discharge a little and it clears.\n- Large gap / no output: open the app and turn the discharge switch back ON.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENS\nMeasurement point differences and BMS protection states explain the small gap; a software-disabled discharge explains the large one.\n\nHOW TO AVOID\nKnow which value you're reading, and check the app's discharge toggle before assuming a hardware fault.",
