      "sub": "Troubleshooting",
      "issue": "Battery constantly shuts down / cuts out during use",
      "summary": "Load rated or surge power exceeds the battery's rating (protection trips), or loose terminals / high resistance. Reduce load or size up; tighten and clean.",
      "template": "WHAT'S HAPPENING\nThe battery keeps cutting output mid-use, sometimes recovering then tripping again.\n\nHOW TO DIAGNOSE\n1. Compare the load's rated AND startup-peak power to the battery's continuous/peak rating. Motors, ACs, pumps surge 2-5× their rated draw.\n2. Inspect terminals for looseness/corrosion and check cable gauge.\n3. For inverter setups, check the inverter isn't tripping its own protection (over-temp, low-voltage).\n\nFIX\n- Reduce the operating load or move to a battery with higher continuous/peak output.\n- Tighten and clean terminals; ensure cable gauge meets the device's current.\n- Improve ventilation if over-temp protection is involved.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENS\nThe BMS trips over-current/over-temp protection when the demand or resistance exceeds safe limits, then re-arms — producing the on/off cycle.\n\nHOW TO AVOID\nSize the battery for surge loads, use correct cabling, keep connections tight, and allow airflow around the battery and any inverter.",
