      "template": "WHAT'S HAPPENING\nThe app or phone won't connect to the battery's Bluetooth.\n\nFIRST QUESTION — is it a brand-new, never-used battery?\n- NEW / UNUSED: the battery may be asleep from shipping/storage. Ask the customer to APPLY A LOAD (or connect a charger) to wake it, then immediately try connecting via Bluetooth. Many 'won't connect out of the box' cases are simply a dormant pack — activity wakes the Bluetooth module. If it connects after applying load, done.\n- IN-USE / OLDER battery, or still failing after waking it: run the troubleshooting below.\n\nHOW TO DIAGNOSE / FIX (in-use battery)\n1. Confirm the battery is turned ON — if it's off, its Bluetooth can't broadcast.\n2. Turn the phone's Bluetooth OFF then ON; reopen the app and search again.\n3. Move the phone close (within ~10m, fewer walls in between).\n4. Make sure no other phone is already holding the connection — Bluetooth pairs one device at a time.\n5. Use the app's 'Search Nearby' to see if the device's Bluetooth name appears; if so, connect/add it.\n6. If still failing: drain the battery until the device turns off, then recharge and turn it on — this restarts the Bluetooth module. Retry the steps.\n7. Android only: the app needs Location permission to scan for Bluetooth — it doesn't store location.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENS\nA dormant new pack, the battery being off, the phone's Bluetooth stack, distance/obstacles, another phone holding the link, or a module that needs a restart.\n\nHOW TO AVOID\nWake a new battery with a load/charger before pairing, keep the battery on and nearby, and only connect one phone at a time.",
