      "template": "WHAT'S HAPPENING\nThe battery accepts charge fine but delivers nothing to the load.\n\nHOW TO DIAGNOSE\n1. Is a charger connected? If load power < charger output, the charger powers the load directly and the battery simply isn't discharging — not a fault.\n2. Bluetooth model: is the discharge switch OFF in the app?\n3. Check the app for any protection/abnormal flags.\n\nFIX\n- Compare load power to charger output (output = charge voltage × charge current). If the load runs and the battery isn't needed, it's normal.\n- Turn the discharge switch ON in the app.\n- Try turning the battery off and back on via the app; if needed, rebind the app.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENS\nUsually a software-disabled discharge or a charger masking the battery's role — genuine 'won't discharge' hardware faults are rarer.\n\nHOW TO AVOID\nLeave the discharge switch enabled in normal use, and remember a connected charger can cover small loads on its own.",
