      "template": "WHAT'S HAPPENING\nCharging keeps stopping and restarting, or the battery repeatedly drops off the charger.\n\nHOW TO DIAGNOSE\n1. Charger type — LiFePO4 or a device with lithium mode (MPPT/DCDC)?\n2. Charge voltage — within range? 12V: 14.2-14.6V; 24V/36V/48V = ×2/×3/×4.\n3. Connections tight and un-oxidised?\n\nFIX\n- Switch to a correct LiFePO4 charger set to the right voltage.\n- Tighten/clean terminals.\n- If the over-voltage protection keeps tripping, lower the charge voltage to spec.\n\nWHY IT HAPPENS\nToo-high charge voltage makes the BMS trip over-voltage protection, which clears and re-trips, producing the cycling.\n\nHOW TO AVOID\nUse a properly configured LiFePO4 charger and verify the voltage matches the pack before charging.",
